      "documentId": "doc_cbc_nov",
      "summary": "What your report states:\nYour November 2026 panel lists Hemoglobin at 12.1 g/dL (reference 13.0–17.0 g/dL, marked Low), Fasting Blood Glucose at 106 mg/dL (reference 70–99 mg/dL, marked High), HbA1c at 6.1% (reference 4.0–5.6%, marked High), and Potassium at 4.3 mmol/L (within 3.5–5.1 mmol/L, Normal). Vitamin B12 is 285 pg/mL with no printed reference range, so it is marked Unable to Classify.\n\nPlain-language explanation:\nCompared to your August 2026 report, Fasting Glucose (118 to 106 mg/dL) and HbA1c (6.4% to 6.1%) moved lower while remaining above the printed reference limit. Hemoglobin is slightly below the lab reference minimum. Because Vitamin B12 lacks a printed reference range on this sheet, it is not assumed normal. Please review all findings with your physician.",
